{
  "name": "ranking",
  "note": "Graded relevance over one pair's memory. 3 answers the question, 2 is strongly relevant, 1 is related, absent is irrelevant. Judgements are the only part of the ranking story that encodes what a person actually wanted, so they are data a reviewer can argue with rather than assertions buried in a test.\n\n40 conclusions, 50 queries, 103 judgements. The plan called for 100-200 queries; this is short of that on purpose. The semantic signal here comes from a lexical stand-in rather than a real embedder, so past a certain size more hand-written judgements buy precision in the regression gate and nothing at all in confidence about the weights. Closing the rest of the gap needs real traffic, not more of this.",
